+   object-cover, sizes="100vw", srcset to 1920w) with a GSAP entrance push-in
+   and a scrubbed parallax. PageHero/HomeHero are rebuilt around it: eyebrow ->
+   H1 -> tagline -> two CTAs -> slim fact rail, copy bottom-anchored on phones,
+   min-h-[100svh] so browser chrome can never crop it, desktop-only spec card.
+   The crowded `chips` hero prop is gone from the API and all 13 call sites.
+
+2. GSAP on scroll and on the header. Header: staggered entrance, a quickTo
+   underline pill that follows hover/focus, a ScrollTrigger shrink that also
+   eases the brand mark to scale .9, and an animated mobile drawer with accordion
+   groups. New motion-extra.tsx adds a scroll-velocity-reactive Marquee and
+   RuleDraw; reveals now stagger service bullets, both pricing tables and all
+   FAQ lists. Above-the-fold entrance states are set in CSS under a double gate
+   (.js-anim + prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) with an anim-safety
+   fallback, so nothing flashes in on load or gets stuck hidden.
+
+3. Logo sync - two real bugs fixed. (a) The export path used create +
+   joinChannel where the trailing resize() was a no-op, so every asset carried
+   the artwork shrunk into a corner; rebuilt by resizing the alpha mask first
+   and painting flat, each file verified by ink box against the source.
+   (b) The header was showing the official monogram beside a wordmark I had
+   re-typeset in Bitter; new qp-lockup-h-*.png composites the monogram with the
+   artwork's own two wordmark lines into one image, and both tones cross-fade so
+   the bar can go solid on scroll without the logo snapping between files. Only
+   the visible tone preloads. Favicon, apple-icon, PWA icon and the 1200x630 OG
+   card are regenerated from the corrected assets.
+
+Also: minimalist pass (hairline-ruled blocks instead of bordered cards, softened
