+## What this does
+
+Follow-up to the merged redesign (#1) — the three things the review asked for after it landed.
+
+### 1. The hero image is now the banner
+
+`HeroBackdrop` renders each page's own photograph **full-bleed behind the copy at every breakpoint** (`fill` + `object-cover`, `sizes="100vw"`, srcset served to 1920w) with a GSAP entrance push-in and a scrubbed parallax. `PageHero`/`HomeHero` are rebuilt around it: eyebrow → H1 → tagline → two CTAs → slim fact rail, copy bottom-anchored on phones over the darker half of the photo, `min-h-[100svh]` so browser chrome can never crop it, desktop-only spec card. The crowded `chips` hero prop is gone from the API and all 13 call sites.
+
+### 2. GSAP on scroll and on the header
+
+- **Header:** staggered entrance, a `gsap.quickTo` underline pill that follows hover/focus, a `ScrollTrigger` shrink that also eases the brand mark to `scale: .9`, and an animated mobile drawer with accordion groups.
+- **Scroll:** new `motion-extra.tsx` adds a scroll-velocity-reactive `Marquee` and `RuleDraw`; reveals now stagger service bullets, both pricing tables and all 90+ FAQ items.
+- Above-the-fold entrance states are set in CSS under a double gate (`.js-anim` **and** `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`) with an `anim-safety` fallback — so the bar can't flash in on load, can't get stuck hidden if the JS chunk fails, and no-JS visitors and crawlers always see the finished markup.
+
+### 3. Logo sync — two real bugs fixed
+
+1. **Extraction bug.** The export path used `create` + `joinChannel`, where the trailing `.resize()` was a silent no-op, so every asset carried the artwork shrunk into a corner of its canvas. Rebuilt by resizing the alpha mask first, then painting flat — every file is verified by measuring its ink box against the source.
+2. **The header wasn't using the logo's letterforms.** It paired the official monogram with a wordmark re-typeset in the site's display font, which is what read as "out of sync". New `qp-lockup-h-*.png` composites the monogram with the artwork's own two wordmark lines into a single image; the header renders that, and both tones cross-fade so the bar can go solid on scroll without the logo snapping between files. Only the visible tone preloads.
+
+Favicon, apple-icon, PWA icon, manifest icons and the 1200×630 OG card are all regenerated from the corrected assets.
+
+### Also in here
+
+- **Minimalist pass:** hairline-ruled blocks instead of bordered cards (`ServiceCard`, `ProcessSteps`, `RelatedServices`, `TrustBadges`, `Testimonials`, the home steps/stats), softened shadows, ticker reduced from 32 logo copies to a two-copy seamless loop. All pricing, form numbers, FAQs and CTAs unchanged.
+- **Brand assets are now reproducible:** `brand/qp-logo-source.png` (the official artwork, untouched) and `brand/export-brand-assets.mjs` ship with the repo. `node brand/export-brand-assets.mjs` re-derives all ten assets plus icons and OG card, prints an ink-box check per file, and exits non-zero on any mismatch.
+- `package.json` lint swapped from the removed `next lint` to `tsc --noEmit` (Next 16 dropped the wrapper).
+- `manifest.ts` no longer references the deleted `icon.svg`; `buildMetadata` declares 1200×630 for `/images/brand/*` instead of the page-banner 1376×860, so the declared `og:image` size always matches the file.
+- README warns against running `npm run build` while `npm run dev` is serving `.next` (that is what caused the earlier "pages not loading").
+
+## Verification
+
+- 31 routes return 200 over HTTP (`/`, all 12 service pages, both factoring sub-pages, 7 insight slugs, store, faq, about, contact, get-started, insurance, privacy-policy, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, `manifest.webmanifest`, `icon.png`).
+- `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`) → exit 0.
+- Brand assets: ink-box checks pass on all ten files (mark 645×645, stacked 966×1110, lockup 1713×645, wordmark 966×327 at 3×); re-running the export reproduces the committed assets.
+- Reduced-motion and no-JS paths checked in the SSR markup and the compiled CSS.
+
+## Review note
+
+`REDESIGN-NOTES.md` §2.1 and §3 document the logo system and the full animation inventory, including the "never hand-set the wordmark in a font" rule that this PR establishes.
